<!--
~/.codex/session_context.md — Persistent Session Memory (PSM).

A small, hand-curated file the agent reads at the start of every session to
recover cross-session context that does not belong in any one repo. Keep it
SHORT (it is prepended to context). Prune ruthlessly; this is working memory,
not an archive. The PSM-sync hook (claude-integration) can append timestamped
notes here automatically.
-->

# Session Context (PSM)

## Who / What
- Operator: <your name / handle>
- Primary goal this period: <one line>

## Active threads
<!-- 3-7 bullets max. Each: what it is + the very next action. -->
- <project>: <state> → next: <action>

## Durable preferences
<!-- Things the agent should always honor across repos. -->
- Commit style: <e.g. Conventional Commits, imperative mood>
- Always run tests before declaring done.
- Ask before destructive git ops.

## Known pitfalls / scar tissue
<!-- Hard-won lessons so they are not repeated. -->
- <gotcha> → <how to avoid>

## Parking lot
<!-- Ideas to revisit; not active. -->
- <idea>

